            <ArticleTitle>An approach to the patient with unexplained chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>331, 333</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After coronary artery disease has been excluded as a cause for unexplained chest pain, oesophageal disease must be considered. Ambulatory pH monitoring reveals abnormal oesophageal acid exposure in 50% of patients with recurrent non-cardiac chest pain.</AbstractText>
